t table. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>uint32_t *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">sourceTable<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">The address of the source vector table.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">sourceSize<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A number of entries in the source vector table.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint32_t *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">targetTable<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">The address of the target (new) vector table.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>uint32_t<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">targetSize<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">A number of entries in the target vector table.<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>void *<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">defaultHandler<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">An address of the interrupt handler used for target entries for which where there is no corresponding source entry (i.e., the target table is larger than the source table).<\/p><\/td><\/tr><tr><td>bool<\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">overwriteActive<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">When true, a target table entry is always overwritten with the corresponding source entry. If false, a target table entry is only overwritten if it is zero. This makes it possible for an application to partly initialize a target table before passing it to this function. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">This function will set a new VTOR register value.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>CORE_CriticalDisableIrq<span id=\"core-critical-disable-irq\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#core-critical-disable-irq\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void CORE_CriticalDisableIrq (void )<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Disable interrupts. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>void<\/td><td>N/A<\/td><td class=\"paramname\"><\/td><td><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">Disable all interrupts by setting PRIMASK. (Fault exception handlers will still be enabled). <\/p><br><\/div><div><h3>CORE_CriticalEnableIrq<span id=\"core-critical-enable-irq\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#core-critical-enable-irq\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void CORE_CriticalEnableIrq (void )<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable interrupts. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>void<\/td><td>N/A<\/td><td class=\"paramname\"><\/td><td><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable interrupts by clearing PRIMASK. <\/p><br><\/div><div><h3>CORE_ExitCritical<span id=\"core-exit-critical\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#core-exit-critical\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void CORE_ExitCritical (<a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/4.4.6/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/core#core-irq-state-t-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">CORE_irqState_t<\/a> irqState)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Exit a CRITICAL section. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td><a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/4.4.6/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/core#core-irq-state-t-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">CORE_irqState_t<\/a><\/td><td>[in]<\/td><td class=\"paramname\">irqState<\/td><td><p style=\"color:inherit\">The interrupt priority blocking level to restore to PRIMASK when exiting the CRITICAL section. This value is usually the one returned by a prior call to <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/4.4.6/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/core#core-enter-critical\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">CORE_EnterCritical()<\/a>. <\/p><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><br><\/div><div><h3>CORE_YieldCritical<span id=\"core-yield-critical\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#core-yield-critical\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void CORE_YieldCritical (void )<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Brief interrupt enable/disable sequence to allow handling of pending interrupts. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>void<\/td><td>N/A<\/td><td class=\"paramname\"><\/td><td><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">Usually used within a CRITICAL section. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>CORE_EnterCritical<span id=\"core-enter-critical\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#core-enter-critical\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>CORE_irqState_t CORE_EnterCritical (void )<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enter a CRITICAL section. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>void<\/td><td>N/A<\/td><td class=\"paramname\"><\/td><td><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">When a CRITICAL section is entered, all interrupts (except fault handlers) are disabled.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Returns<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">The value of PRIMASK register prior to the CRITICAL section entry. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>CORE_AtomicDisableIrq<span id=\"core-atomic-disable-irq\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#core-atomic-disable-irq\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void CORE_AtomicDisableIrq (void )<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Disable interrupts. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>void<\/td><td>N/A<\/td><td class=\"paramname\"><\/td><td><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">Disable interrupts with a priority lower or equal to <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/4.4.6/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/core#core-atomic-base-priority-level\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">CORE_ATOMIC_BASE_PRIORITY_LEVEL<\/a>. Sets core BASEPRI register to CORE_ATOMIC_BASE_PRIORITY_LEVEL.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">If <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/4.4.6/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/core#core-atomic-method\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">CORE_ATOMIC_METHOD<\/a> is <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/4.4.6/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/core#core-atomic-method-primask\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">CORE_ATOMIC_METHOD_PRIMASK<\/a>, this function is identical to <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/4.4.6/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/core#core-critical-disable-irq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">CORE_CriticalDisableIrq()<\/a>. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>CORE_AtomicEnableIrq<span id=\"core-atomic-enable-irq\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#core-atomic-enable-irq\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void CORE_AtomicEnableIrq (void )<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable interrupts. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Parameters<\/strong><table><thead><tr><th>Type<\/th><th>Direction<\/th><th>Argument Name<\/th><th>Description<\/th><\/tr><\/thead><tbody><tr><td>void<\/td><td>N/A<\/td><td class=\"paramname\"><\/td><td><\/td><\/tr><\/tbody><\/table><\/div><p style=\"color:inherit\">Enable interrupts by setting core BASEPRI register to 0.<\/p><p style=\"color:inherit\"><strong>Note<\/strong><\/p><ul style=\"list-style:\"><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">If <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/4.4.6/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/core#core-atomic-method\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">CORE_ATOMIC_METHOD<\/a> is <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/4.4.6/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/core#core-atomic-method-basepri\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">CORE_ATOMIC_METHOD_BASEPRI<\/a> and PRIMASK is set (CPU is inside a CRITICAL section), interrupts will still be disabled after calling this function.<\/p><\/li><li><p style=\"color:inherit\">If <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/4.4.6/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/core#core-atomic-method\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">CORE_ATOMIC_METHOD<\/a> is <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/4.4.6/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/core#core-atomic-method-primask\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">CORE_ATOMIC_METHOD_PRIMASK<\/a>, this function is identical to <a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/4.4.6/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/core#core-critical-enable-irq\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">CORE_CriticalEnableIrq()<\/a>. <\/p><\/li><\/ul><br><\/div><div><h3>CORE_ExitAtomic<span id=\"core-exit-atomic\" class=\"self-anchor\"><a class=\"perm\" href=\"#core-exit-atomic\">#<\/a><\/span><\/h3><blockquote>void CORE_ExitAtomic (<a href=\"http://docs.silabs.com/gecko-platform/4.4.6/platform-emlib-efr32xg22/core#core-irq-state-t-1\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"\">CORE_irqState_t<\/a> irqState)<\/blockquote><p style=\"color:inherit\">Exit an ATOMIC section. <\/p><div class=\"parameters-section\"><strong class=\"parameters\">Paramet